index a92d0d12..12c8f59b 100644
--- a/docs/internals/chipset.md
+++ b/docs/internals/chipset.md
@@ -503,3 +503,22 @@ Deliberate non-goals, recorded so they are not re-investigated: A2024 /
 UHRES dual-scan display (a one-time "not emulated" warning is kept),
 genlock ZD output beyond register storage, and AGA "double CAS"
 memory-timing fidelity beyond what `timing-test/` measurements justify.
+
+### A500 single/dual playfield collision checks
+
+Live CLXDAT bit0 compares the CLXCON-enabled odd/even plane matches; it does
+not require visible nonzero pixels or dual-playfield mode. Zero-valued samples
+can satisfy a zero match value, and disabled match planes do not constrain it.
+Sprite?PF1 matching differs: single-playfield mode also requires the even-plane
+match, while dual-playfield mode permits the odd match independently. The paired
+A500 matrix found no corresponding mode difference in sprite?PF2 or bit0.
+
+The consensus fixture `src/bus/tests/data/a500_playfield_modes.csv` comes from
+two independent512-case runs on a PAL A500, two repeats per condition. It covers
+two lores planes, four constant data patterns, four CLXCON enable masks and
+four desired values, sprite0 on/off, and DPF off/on. The probe begins with zero
+BPLDAT before constant DMA output. Source and full references are versioned in
+`amiga-hardware-probes/references/playfield-modes-v1`; ROM SHA256 is
+`3a614aba9686ad37d83a210a0016b6ec870e36d1fa07294ba0e4ab0c31d82765`.
+This pins collision logic for those conditions, not all sprite, AGA, or early
+DMA timing behavior.
